const LANGNOTE={"Modern Standard Arabic":"Covers Lebanese and Iraqi communities with no prior toll concept. RTL layout. Mosque and community-org networks, Arabic radio. NSW: Lakemba, Bankstown, Auburn, Merrylands.","Vietnamese":"Highest low-English rate of any major group. Scam-wary of digital; trusts community radio (SBS Vietnamese), Facebook groups, physical mail. NSW: Cabramatta (2166), Fairfield. VIC: Springvale. QLD: Inala (4077).","Simplified Chinese":"WeChat and RedNote are the dominant channels. Corridor proficiency below state average. NSW +197k, VIC +170k, QLD +61k net China arrivals since 2021. QLD: Sunnybank.","Traditional Chinese":"Separate written deliverable from Simplified. WeChat, Chinese-language press. Also serves Traditional-reading Chinese-Vietnamese. QLD: Sunnybank, Robertson.","Assyrian Neo-Aramaic":"Do not assume Arabic covers this community. Consult on preferred channel before commissioning. Elders: church networks, audio/video. NSW: Fairfield (2165), Smithfield (2164/2176).","Chaldean Neo-Aramaic":"Consult before assuming Arabic coverage. Church and community-org networks. Concentrated with Assyrian in NSW Fairfield/Smithfield.","Farsi":"One written deliverable serves Iranian (Farsi), Afghan Dari and Hazaragi. 2021 figures understate the post-2021 Afghan cohort: NOM Afghanistan +29,750 VIC, +17,260 NSW.","Khmer":"Cambodia has no toll road system. Older refugee-background cohort, interrupted schooling. Temple networks, audio first. VIC: Springvale/Noble Park. NSW: Fairfield.","Korean":"Low/no English well below state average. KakaoTalk and community channels; shame-sensitive. NSW: Strathfield. QLD: Sunnybank/Robertson.","Turkish":"VIC fourth-largest corridor language, stronger than statewide. Turkish radio and community orgs. Meadow Heights/Jacana, Broadmeadows. Strong vulnerability signal.","Nepali":"High English (4% low/no). Priority is toll-concept unfamiliarity, not language: Nepal has no toll roads. Fast-growing: NOM +131,930 NSW. Outreach over translation.","Punjabi":"High English (7.7-9.9% low/no). Digital, friend-network led, gurdwara networks, strong Punjabi radio. Fast-growing (NOM India). Outreach and framing over translation.","Somali":"Horn of Africa: roads are free. Higher proportional corridor presence in QLD (1.1%). Audio/video and community orgs. Education before enforcement.","Tigrinya":"Horn of Africa, no toll concept. Variable first-language literacy. Audio/video and church/community networks. Melbourne and Brisbane western suburbs.","Samoan":"Pacific: no toll concept. High English (10% low/no). Church and collectivist networks. Priority is toll-concept outreach, not translation. QLD 1.7%.","Spanish":"Diverse origins, mixed toll familiarity. High English (~87% proficient). Lower priority than Arabic in QLD."};
