 prevent:{label:"Prevent",color:"var(--teal)",intro:"NAT has not yet occurred, or has just happened without an account. Equip people to open an account and keep it active — entry may be proactive (settlement, licensing) or reactive (a first notice).",
  stages:[{n:1,name:"First contact",ctx:"First encounter with the toll system",happening:"No account and no prior understanding. Entry is proactive (settlement, orientation, licensing) or reactive (a first notice arrives).",msg:"Tolls work differently here — but help is available, in your language, and the system is on your side.",tps:["Settlement orientation","Licensing","TAFE / uni orientation","Toll notice"]},{n:2,name:"Awareness & understanding",ctx:"Learning what tolling is",happening:"Making sense of tolls from settlement services, community contacts, family, or a notice.",msg:"An account is free to hold and works in the background — it protects you from larger one-off costs.",tps:["Community org session","WhatsApp / WeChat / Facebook","Driving school","Community champions"]},{n:3,name:"Capability",ctx:"Able and confident to set up",happening:"Understands what an account is; needs to feel able to set one up. Worries about ongoing costs and data security.",msg:"Setting up takes a few minutes, and someone can sit with you — no English phone call required.",tps:["Family member","In-person setup at a community org","Linkt app (Easy English)","In-language chat"]},{n:4,name:"Commitment",ctx:"Deciding to act",happening:"Ready to act, prompted by a settlement worker, family member, life moment, or a deadline.",msg:"You've got this — and if anything is unclear, you can ask for an interpreter at no cost.",tps:["Settlement worker prompt","Life-event trigger","Notice deadline"]},{n:5,name:"Action",ctx:"Completing setup",happening:"Completes setup or responds to the notice. Needs clear confirmation it worked and what's next.",msg:"You're set up. Here's what happens next, and how to check your account any time.",tps:["Confirmation in-language","Account dashboard","Follow-up reassurance"]}]},
 resolve:{label:"Resolve",color:"#3E6BB0",intro:"Overdue tolls are understood and resolved before they escalate. The focus is supporting people to respond at first contact — before the situation compounds.",
  stages:[{n:1,name:"Notice contact",ctx:"The notice is the first contact that matters",happening:"An unpaid notice arrives. The tone of this moment shapes everything. CALD audiences are more likely to resolve a first invoice — if the path feels safe.",msg:"This can be sorted out. The notice assumes you meant to do the right thing — because most people do.",tps:["The notice itself","SMS (not email)","In-language community platforms"]},{n:2,name:"Understanding",ctx:"Making sense of what to do",happening:"Working out why the notice came and the options. Shame and confusion can suppress action; many will not call.",msg:"Here's what happened and your options — in plain language, in your language.",tps:["In-language guided chat & FAQs","Linkt app (Easy English)","Community workers"]},{n:3,name:"Resolution",ctx:"Resolving and fixing the cause",happening:"Resolving in a single contact, in-language without long waits, and fixing the account configuration so it doesn't recur. Compliance history counts.",msg:"Let's resolve this in one go — and set things up so it doesn't happen again.",tps:["In-app chat, in-language","One-off payment (no account)","Recognition of compliance history"]},{n:4,name:"Action & repair",ctx:"Resolved, set to prevent recurrence",happening:"Notice resolved; direct debit and top-up notifications set up. The experience travels through the driver's network next.",msg:"Done. Your account is set up to catch issues early from here.",tps:["Direct debit & top-up alerts","Account settings made easy","Driver communities"]}]},
 amplify:{label:"Amplify",color:"#6D28D9",intro:"Confident users with healthy accounts have the motivation and knowledge to help others. The challenge is not motivation but activation. Transurban's role is to enable, not to lead.",
  stages:[{n:1,name:"Awareness",ctx:"Recognising their experience is useful",happening:"Established in their community, often the person others come to for advice. Accounts feel unremarkable — they may not see that what they know is valuable.",msg:"A quick check when life changes keeps things on track — and what you know helps people around you.",tps:["Proactive alerts in-language","Loyalty milestones","Rideshare / gig partnerships"]},{n:2,name:"Understanding",ctx:"Knowing what to share, with whom",happening:"Helping others navigate unfamiliar systems is a social norm, not a marketing act. Shame norms can suppress open conversation.",msg:"Toll confusion is more common than people think — someone in your network may be struggling quietly.",tps:["Conversation-normalisation content","Life-event prompts"]},{n:3,name:"Capability",ctx:"Something concrete to pass on",happening:"Willing to help, but with nothing ready to forward in the right language or format. Without something concrete, it stays verbal and doesn't scale.",msg:"Hearing how, from someone you trust, means more than any website — here's something easy to send on.",tps:["Multilingual shareables (WhatsApp / WeChat)","Family account features","Community Champion program"]},{n:4,name:"Action",ctx:"Actively sharing and helping",happening:"Actively helping others. The system recognises and rewards their role — the benefit flows both ways.",msg:"If someone you know needs help, they can call Linkt Assist and ask for an interpreter at no cost.",tps:["Community Champion program","Loyalty programme","Transurban funds, equips, then steps back"]}]},
